  { q: 'Will my cylinder cope with a new en-suite?', a: 'If it is vented, adding another bathroom often shows up the low pressure. We check the hot water at every bathroom survey and tell you if an upgrade is needed. The en-suite and cylinder can go on one fixed price.' },
  { q: 'Are your engineers G3 qualified?', a: 'Yes. All our engineers are G3 qualified to fit and service unvented cylinders. The work is notified as the Building Regulations require, and you get the paperwork to keep. Makers need this paperwork for the warranty.' },
  { q: 'How long does a cylinder swap take?', a: 'Most swaps are done in one day. A change from vented to unvented can take a little longer. We tell you at the survey.' },
  { q: 'How much is a new immersion heater in Formby?', a: 'An immersion heater on a vented cylinder is £175 including VAT. On an unvented cylinder it is £275. Both are supplied and fitted, and are often done the same day.' },
  { q: 'Does an unvented cylinder need a yearly service?', a: 'Yes. Makers ask for a yearly service to keep the warranty valid. It also checks the safety valves still work. Our unvented cylinder service is £120 including VAT.' },
  { q: 'Are you Gas Safe registered?', a: 'Yes. Gas work is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. You can check any engineer on the Gas Safe Register before they start.' },
];
